# Week 02: 3D Wing Geometry & Vortex-Lattice Method (VLM)

## 🎯 Objective
Design a 3D main wing planform based on the NACA 4412 profile and evaluate spanwise lift distribution, induced drag, and Oswald efficiency using XFLR5's Vortex-Lattice Method (VLM1 / VLM2).

---

## 📐 Wing Planform Architecture

* **Wingspan ($b$):** $2.0 \text{ m}$
* **Root Chord ($c_{\text{root}}$):** $0.18 \text{ m}$
* **Tip Chord ($c_{\text{tip}}$):** $0.11 \text{ m}$
* **Taper Ratio ($\lambda$):** $0.61$
* **Mean Aerodynamic Chord ($c_{\text{MAC}}$):** $0.145 \text{ m}$
* **Planform Area ($S_{\text{ref}}$):** $0.29 \text{ m}^2$
* **Aspect Ratio ($AR$):** $13.8$
* **Geometric Twist:** $-2.0^\circ$ (Washout at tip to mitigate tip stall)

